// The jobs done most often in the menus, and the most actions each may take
// (#236). An action is one press: a click, or a key going down. A budget is
// a ceiling, not a target: never cut an action at the cost of the player
// understanding or being safe (docs/philosophy/menus.md, Count the clicks).
//
//   name      the job, as docs/click-budget.md names it.
//   from      where the player is when the count starts.
//   mouse     the most presses with the pointer.
//   keys      the most presses with the keyboard.
//   waits_on  the issue that will make the job possible. A job with one
//             cannot be walked yet and has no measured count.
//
// The walk (procedures/walk-the-click-budget.txt) does each job that can be
// done in the running game, both ways, and says which are over.
// The budgets are the owner's: these were set by her on 2026-10-11, after
// the first walk.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
(
    jobs: [
        (
            name: "Equip an upgrade the report just showed",
            from: "In town, the Journal open on the report.",
            mouse: 2,
            keys: 2,
        ),
        (
            name: "List everything not wanted",
            from: "In town, Horses open on Gear.",
            mouse: 3,
            keys: 3,
            waits_on: 99,
        ),
        (
            name: "Give a horse a different ability",
            from: "In town, Horses open on Gear.",
            mouse: 3,
            keys: 3,
        ),
        (
            name: "Set out for the next town",
            from: "In town, any place open.",
            mouse: 1,
            keys: 1,
        ),
        (
            name: "Find out why a piece was left behind",
            from: "In town, Horses open on Gear.",
            mouse: 2,
            keys: 2,
        ),
        (
            name: "Find out why something did not sell",
            from: "In town, Horses open on Gear.",
            mouse: 2,
            keys: 2,
            waits_on: 170,
        ),
    ],
)
